From 00f75d433c79f13332c7eeb9d11f54b981e3b9c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:53:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: TEMPORARY stall-locator diagnostic (STALLDBG.LOG)

REMOVAL IS PLANNED, NOT OPTIONAL: this patch exists to answer one open
question and must be reverted once it has. It is landed separately from
the pacer fix (0030) precisely so it can be removed without touching
anything load-bearing -- per the hub convention that a temporary
diagnostic patch needs its removal planned at landing time rather than
left as an unscheduled follow-up.

WHY: the port sits at 14.936fps against a hard 15.000fps ceiling
(lockedFrameRate=15 makes the pacer's deadline exactly 66.6667ms, so the
average can approach but never exceed it). Steady-state is already
14.9989fps with the pacer landing on its deadline within microseconds.
The entire remaining shortfall is 3-4 discrete stall frames per run, at
FIXED frame positions, reproducible regardless of player input.

An earlier revision of this diagnostic timed render+flip and the audio
pump, and produced a sharp negative: 16 stall lines, ALL inside frames
0-21 (startup), and NOTHING at the mid-run stall around frames
1800-2100 -- even though the pacer's own instrumentation confirmed that
stall occurred on the same run (~333ms). Since the detector was verified
to fire, that silence is evidence: the startup stall and the mid-run
stall are NOT the same bug, and the mid-run one spends its ~330ms
outside the render/flip/pump span entirely.

WHAT: adds a tail_ms field covering the only remaining span -- the loop
tail between the frame pacer and the end of the loop body (game logic,
movement, aging, chest checks, event polling). Logs on either a slow
work span (>100ms) or a slow tail (>50ms).

Costs a normal frame five clock reads and NO file I/O; it writes only
when a frame is anomalously slow, which is a handful of lines per run.
That restraint is deliberate -- unconditional per-frame logging was
measured at 0.70ms/frame (SDL/0136) and ~0.4-0.5fps (patch 0028), enough
to swamp the effect being measured.

Detector verified to fire before use, both revisions: thresholds
lowered, well-formed output confirmed, thresholds restored, rebuilt. A
silent detector and a broken one are indistinguishable, and this one is
specifically being used to interpret a silence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gameSource/game.cpp | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 51 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gameSource/game.cpp b/gameSource/game.cpp
index 3a56a49..652dd84 100644
--- a/gameSource/game.cpp
+++ b/gameSource/game.cpp
@@ -1149,7 +1149,23 @@ char playGame() {
 
     while( !done ) {
 
-        
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+        // TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC (STALLDBG.LOG): locate the w7-class stall.
+        //
+        // A previous round instrumented render+flip+pump and produced a
+        // sharp result: 16 stall lines, ALL inside frames 0-21 (the startup
+        // window), and NOTHING at w7 -- even though PACEDBG confirmed w7's
+        // usual ~333ms stall happened on that same run. The detector was
+        // proven to fire, so that silence is evidence rather than absence:
+        // whatever costs w7 its ~330ms is NOT in the render/flip/pump span.
+        //
+        // This extends coverage to the only remaining span -- the loop tail
+        // (game logic, movement, aging, chest checks, event polling) between
+        // the pacer and the end of the loop body. Logs on EITHER a slow work
+        // span or a slow tail, so whichever one w7 lives in, it surfaces.
+        const Uint64 stallT0 = SDL_GetTicksNS();
+#endif
+
         if( getKeyDown( SDL_SCANCODE_S ) ) {
             stepDX = false;
             }
@@ -1399,6 +1415,9 @@ char playGame() {
         
         flipGameImageOntoScreen( screen );
 
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+        const Uint64 stallT1 = SDL_GetTicksNS();   // end render+flip
+#endif
 
 #ifdef __DJGPP__
         // DOS-PORT: top up the audio ring explicitly once per frame,
@@ -1537,6 +1556,10 @@ char playGame() {
 #endif
 
 
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+        const Uint64 stallT2 = SDL_GetTicksNS();   // end audio pump
+#endif
+
         // done with frame
         double newTimestamp = Time::getCurrentTime();
         
@@ -1772,6 +1795,10 @@ char playGame() {
         // start timing next frame
         lastFrameTimeStamp = Time::getCurrentTime();
 
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+        const Uint64 stallT3 = SDL_GetTicksNS();   // pacer done; tail begins
+#endif
+
 
         // DOS-PORT: rest-of-loop-cost timing (was here through patch
         // 0026) served its purpose -- see presentScreen()'s own comment
@@ -2106,6 +2133,29 @@ char playGame() {
             maxExploreScore = exploreScore;
             }
 
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+        {
+            const Uint64 stallT4 = SDL_GetTicksNS();
+            const double workMs = (double)( stallT2 - stallT0 ) / 1000000.0;
+            const double tailMs = (double)( stallT4 - stallT3 ) / 1000000.0;
+
+            if( ( workMs > 100.0 || tailMs > 50.0 ) &&
+                workMs < 10000.0 && tailMs < 10000.0 ) {
+                FILE *sf = fopen( "STALLDBG.LOG", "ab" );
+                if( sf != NULL ) {
+                    fprintf( sf,
+                             "[stall] frame=%d work_ms=%f render_flip_ms=%f "
+                             "pump_ms=%f tail_ms=%f\n",
+                             frameCount, workMs,
+                             (double)( stallT1 - stallT0 ) / 1000000.0,
+                             (double)( stallT2 - stallT1 ) / 1000000.0,
+                             tailMs );
+                    fclose( sf );
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+#endif
+
         }
 
     unsigned long netTime = time( NULL ) - startTime;
